{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint A[1000][1000];\\nint ps[1010][1010];\\n\\ntypedef long long ll;\\n\\nclass PrefixFrequencyWorkspace {\\n  vector<int> keys_;\\n  vector<uint32_t> counts_;\\n  size_t mask_;\\n\\n  static uint32_t hash_key(int key) {\\n    uint32_t x = static_cast<uint32_t>(key);\\n    x ^= x >> 16;\\n    x *= UINT32_C(0x7feb352d);\\n    x ^= x >> 15;\\n    x *= UINT32_C(0x846ca68b);\\n    x ^= x >> 16;\\n    return x;\\n  }\\n\\n  size_t find_slot(int key) const {\\n    size_t slot = static_cast<size_t>(hash_key(key)) & mask_;\\n    while (counts_[slot] != 0 && keys_[slot] != key)\\n      slot = (slot + 1) & mask_;\\n    return slot;\\n  }\\n\\npublic:\\n  explicit PrefixFrequencyWorkspace(size_t max_prefixes) {\\n    size_t capacity = 1;\\n    while (capacity < 2 * max_prefixes)\\n      capacity <<= 1;\\n    keys_.resize(capacity);\\n    counts_.resize(capacity);\\n    mask_ = capacity - 1;\\n  }\\n\\n  void reset() {\\n    // Independent contiguous stores permit vectorized or bulk clearing.\\n    fill(counts_.begin(), counts_.end(), uint32_t(0));\\n    increment(0);\\n  }\\n\\n  uint32_t count(int key) const {\\n    // An unsuccessful lookup stops at an empty slot without inserting.\\n    return counts_[find_slot(key)];\\n  }\\n\\n  void increment(int key) {\\n    const size_t slot = find_slot(key);\\n    if (counts_[slot] == 0)\\n      keys_[slot] = key;\\n    ++counts_[slot];\\n  }\\n};\\n\\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\\n  for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\\n      ps[i][j] = A[i - 1][j - 1] + ps[i][j - 1];\\n    }\\n  }\\n  PrefixFrequencyWorkspace h(static_cast<size_t>(m) + 1);\\n  ll ans = 0;\\n  for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) // O(m*n^2)\\n    for (int l = j; l <= n; l++) {\\n      h.reset();\\n      int s = 0;\\n      // Both the prefix recurrence and frequency updates remain ordered.\\n      for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\\n        s += ps[i][l] - ps[i][j - 1];\\n        ans += h.count(s - k);\\n        h.increment(s);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  return ans;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n  int k, m, n;\\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\\n  memset(ps, 0, sizeof ps);\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n      cin >> A[i][j];\\n\\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/main.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Replacing unordered_map with a reusable open-addressed workspace and contiguous, vectorizable count clearing should reduce allocation and lookup overhead while preserving the sequential prefix-frequency dependencies.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Tests the full-clearing variant only. Matrix layout, band orientation, threading and I/O remain unchanged. Workspace state is private to each solve call. No commands or measurements were executed.\",\n  \"research\": {\n    \"queries\": [],\n    \"urls\": []\n  },\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Allocate a power-of-two linear-probing table once per solve, with capacity at least twice m+1 and exact key comparisons.\",\n    \"Use unsigned 32-bit hash mixing, signed 32-bit keys, 32-bit frequencies and a 64-bit answer, within the official bounds.\",\n    \"Clear only the contiguous frequency array with std::fill for SIMD-safe resetting; stale keys are ignored when their frequencies are zero.\",\n    \"Keep prefix accumulation and lookup-before-increment sequential, including for k=0; unsuccessful lookups never insert.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
